# Copy to deploy/market-api.env on the server and fill in. Never committed.
#
# TWO TRAPS, both of which look fine and fail later:
#
#   * NO QUOTES. `docker --env-file` does no shell parsing. It splits at the
#     first `=` and takes the rest literally, so MARKET_SECRET="abc" makes
#     the quotes part of the key — and every like token derived from it.
#   * OMIT a line rather than blanking it. An empty value that looks set is a
#     bad afternoon.

# The HMAC key behind every like and ownership token. At least 32 bytes; the
# service refuses to start on less, because a weak key makes the tokens
# reversible and turns the privacy claim into a false one.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# CHANGING THIS ORPHANS EVERY LIKE. The tokens are derived from it, so a new
# key means nobody has liked anything and nobody owns their own listing.
# Treat it as permanent.
MARKET_SECRET=

# Where the platform publishes the public half of its signing key. The
# default in the binary is this same value; it is written out here so that
# the one thing which silently turns every write into a 401 is visible.
MARKET_JWKS_URL=https://auth.opentabs.app/.well-known/jwks.json

# OpenApps account ids allowed to hide or delete a listing. Comma-separated,
# and normally exactly one — yours. Find it by signing in and reading `sub`
# from the access token.
MARKET_MODERATORS=
